{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>And her father — would he spit in her face?</b> And if her father showed her an angry face, <b>would she not be shamed seven days</b>? All the more so for the Shekhinah — fourteen days. But it is enough for that which follows from the kal va-chomer to be like the subject of the kal va-chomer; therefore too in My reproof <b>she shall be shut up seven days</b> (ibid.; Bava Kamma 25)." "<b>And afterward she shall be gathered.</b> I say: every gathering [אֲסִיפָה] mentioned of metzora'im is so called because he is sent outside the camp, and when he is healed he is gathered back into the camp — therefore אֲסִיפָה is written of him, a term of bringing in."], :book :numbers, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 12, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:10:37.711219971Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}